.TH TUXOFLOOD 6 "2026-11-18" "tuxoflood @VERSION@" "Games"
.SH NAME
tuxoflood \- penguin-themed colour-flood puzzle with a move limit
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B tuxoflood
.RB [ \-\-fullscreen ]
.RB [ \-\-mute ]
.RB [ \-\-lang " " hu | en ]
.RB [ \-\-version ]
.RB [ \-h | \-\-help ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B tuxoflood
is a Flood-It style puzzle. The penguin's area starts in the top-left
corner of a board of coloured tiles. Picking a colour recolours the area,
and every touching tile of that colour joins it. Fill the whole board with
one colour before the move limit runs out; otherwise the level is lost and
starts again on a new board. There is no time limit. The move limit of each
board is the length of the built-in solver's solution (the "penguin par")
plus a few spare moves, which shrink as the levels go up. Boards grow from
6x6 with 3 colours to 26x26 with 16 colours, followed by endless levels.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-fullscreen
Start in fullscreen mode.
.TP
.B \-\-mute
Do not open the audio device (no music, no sound effects).
.TP
.BR \-\-lang " " hu | en
User interface language (default: the saved setting, initially Hungarian).
.TP
.B \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Show a short help text and exit.
.SH CONTROLS
.TP
.B Left click
on a colour button or on any board tile: play that colour
.TP
.BR 1 \(en 9 ", " 0 ", " Q " " W " " E " " R " " T " " Y
play colour 1\(en16
.TP
.B N
new board on the same level
.TP
.B C
colour-blind symbols on/off
.TP
.BR P " or " Esc
pause menu
.TP
.B M
music on/off
.TP
.B S
sound effects on/off
.TP
.B F11
toggle fullscreen
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/tuxoflood/progress.json
progress, statistics, high scores and settings (honours
.BR XDG_DATA_HOME ).
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B TUXOFLOOD_DATA_DIR
override the directory of
.IR progress.json .
